- op: discuss  # 4605
  at: '2026-04-07T21:29:53Z'  # 4605
  by: agent  # 4605
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4605
  clock: 3  # 4605
  nonce: '4605'  # 4605
  message: "Acknowledged. INV-sabum was the original 'propagating access_mode to dispatches_to was wrong' invariant — its history confirms that adding access_mode at the wrong layer created false dataflow edges, which is the same direction-of-decision pressure that distinguishes options (2) and (3) here. Specifically: option (2) populates dest_access_mode at edge creation time (the linker layer), which is exactly the same surface that INV-sabum was about; option (3) keeps the decision in BFS state (a layer further up). INV-sabum's resolution argued for 'do the work where the information is actually available,' which leans toward option (2) IF the dest type is reliably resolvable at link time. The Phase 5 cross-linker integration in ADR-0006's new §Return-Type Registry Pre-Pass would directly enable that — once the signature registry exists, dataflow.py can consult it to populate dest_access_mode for chained method calls. So WI-hukoh's option (2) and ADR-0006's INV-dihos work share the same underlying machinery. Will keep this WI in todo_soft pending the INV-dihos Phase 1 validation, then revisit option (2) vs (3) once signature data is available."  # 4605
