  message: "Closing as done per your approval. ADR-0015 §6.1 now documents:\n\n1. The shipped forward-slice admission rule (WI-saful option 1).\n2. The WI-hukoh Phase A/C telemetry results on 4 repos — option 2's unique contribution is 0 edges, because every edge with dest_access_mode populated also has access_mode=write.\n3. The defer-indefinitely decision with the re-evaluation trigger: when INV-dihos Phase 5 or any future linker begins populating dest_access_mode WITHOUT access_mode=write on ≥1% of annotated edges on any repo, re-run the Phase A telemetry; if would_admit_dst_reader > 0, revisit this decision.\n4. Why option 3 was also not evaluated on real data and when it becomes relevant.\n5. INV-forim as a prerequisite finding that prevented the Phase C data from being falsely-zero for the wrong reason.\n\nPR #2928 (docs-only, merged).\n\n## Artifacts summary (all shipped in this session)\n\n- PR #2918: delete vestigial .agent/last_stop_check.json (INV-jofaf facet 1)\n- PR #2921: forward-dataflow admission-rule telemetry in slice.py (WI-hukoh Phase A)\n- PR #2925: preserve dataflow annotations in 4 linkers (INV-forim)\n- PR #2926: INV-jofaf facet 2 split-state-files + scripts/agent-notes tool + cleanup + auto-sync hang guard\n- PR #2928: this ADR amendment + CHANGELOG (WI-hukoh Phase D)\n\n## Monitor in place\n\nSliceResult.admission_stats.would_admit_dst_reader is live and counts the exact edges that would trigger the re-evaluation. It is a no-op to keep around (no behavior change on slicing, just an integer counter), and it flips from zero to non-zero automatically if any future linker changes the edge annotation shape.\n\n## Closing"  # 008b
